+// JET ROUND (P1). K8-PRE: pixel-seed evidence as an INPUT to the K9 arbitration.
+//
+// THE ARCHITECTURAL FACT THIS UNDOES (FINDINGS_JETPHYS.md, measured on 250 jet events):
+// ChainTargetFlags draws the attach target list from `accepted`, the K9 output, so of the 1,015
+// gate-alive 5-layer chains per jet event only 94.6 are ever OFFERED a pixel seed -- while LST master
+// pixel-confirms its whole T5 pool BEFORE its final selection and takes .778 core efficiency out of
+// pT5 (74.4/evt against our 39.8). We reserved pixel confirmation for chains that had already won the
+// arbitration; master uses it to decide the arbitration. This function is that inversion, and nothing
+// more: it runs the SAME frozen head over the SAME predicate with `candKeep` where `accepted` used to
+// be, and its single publication is the orderSeedBonus term of chains.orderKey().
+//
+// SCORE-ONLY, and that is load-bearing rather than incidental:
+//   * plsBest goes to a SCRATCH buffer. The real plsBestChain -- the -RPSA retirement evidence -- is
+//     still the max over the pairs of ACCEPTED targets only, so not one extra bare-pLS row is
+//     retired. Bare pLS rows are 16.5 TC/evt on jets at .969 non-fake; enlarging that max would have
+//     cost efficiency, silently, on both samples.
+//   * xcPairs is nullptr, so the -XC pass-1 stream and its cap are untouched.
+//   * neither attachPls nor attachLogit is written. Writing attachPls here would be a live BUG:
+//     ChainEmitTCs reads it for every emitted chain and would publish a type-7 row whose pixel seed
+//     was never granted, never contended and never deduped.
+// So the only chain-visible effect of this pass is the ORDER the claim walks its candidates in --
+// candKeep is read and never written, so admission is bit-identical -- and orderSeedBonus == 0 skips
+// the pass entirely, which is what makes both arms of the A/B one binary.
